:false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109108","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109108","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109108.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109108.patch","merged_at":"2026-01-27T15:09:24Z"},"body":"Fixes #109088\r\nBugsquad edit: Fixes #115185\r\n\r\nWhen nothing is collapsed, the stored `id` is empty. Spliting an empty string results in an array containing one empty string, thus creating a non-existing ID. According to #86481, when an ID does not exist, it should fall back to searching by name. But there is no fall back logic in `update_tree()`.\r\n\r\nThe spliting problem could have been avoided, as `ConfigFile` supports `Variant` values. It's unnecessary to manually serialize the array and the numbers inside.\r\n\r\nBut in the end, there is no point storing _both_ the instance ID and the corresponding name. This PR removes the dependency on instance IDs.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine